GithubActions
These actions automate deployment pipelines, and automate build and test processes

 
The workflows are defined on event carine, which is the only branch we have
The pull request is done on that same branch. Not appropriate for production.
The permission granted to the workflow is set on 
action: read. 
contents: read Allow metadata about other workflow, 
and, 
security-events: allows reading of repository contents


the job definition is run on a container with latest ubuntu image

in the steps:
1- the first action is to check the source code
2- the second to set up node.js version 18
3- the third action to install dependencies
4- the fourth is to run the build. The build is piped to true (|| true) to force the build event without scaning the code for vulnerabilities.
5- the fith action is ste to skip the test because we do ot have the test.js file yet
6- sixth action is going to istall eslint that will catch all bad coding and vulnerabilities inside the code. It scans all files with js and ts extension
7- the seventh audit for vulnerabilities
8- the eighth run nodejsscan with file exlusion to see if there is any vulnerabilities



